# Central London house prices: contour maps of median price paid by MSOA,
# year ending March 2023, with the River Thames as an impermeable
# D-BARRIERS barrier, then without it.
#
# Values: median price paid for all dwellings, table 1a of 'HPSSA dataset
#   2: median house prices by middle layer super output area', House price
#   statistics for small areas (HPSSA), Office for National Statistics,
#   release of September 2023 (based on HM Land Registry Price Paid Data).
#   https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/housing/datasets/
#   hpssadataset2medianhousepricebymsoaquarterlyrollingyear
#   Values are in thousands of pounds.
# Locations: MSOA 2011 to 2021 lookup (MSOA11_MSOA21_LAD22_EW_LU_v2) and
#   the centroid fields BNG_E, BNG_N of Middle layer Super Output Areas
#   (December 2021) Boundaries EW BSC V3, ONS Open Geography Portal.
#   https://geoportal.statistics.gov.uk/
# River: River Thames centreline from OS Open Rivers (Ordnance Survey).
#
# Source: Office for National Statistics licensed under the Open
# Government Licence v3.0. Contains HM Land Registry data (c) Crown
# copyright and database right 2023. Contains OS data (c) Crown copyright
# and database right 2021-2026.
#
# Approximations: each MSOA is placed at its 2021 boundary centroid, not
# a population-weighted one; 9 MSOAs changed in 2021 and use the
# centroid of the 2021 MSOA the lookup gives. Points are taken up to
# 1.5 km beyond the window. The Thames is the OS Open Rivers route
# simplified to 80 m, which runs mid-channel; it is drawn as ~ and the
# barrier follows the same vertices, extended 3 km past the window.
# Coordinates are British National Grid kilometres: down from northing
# 183.5 km, across from easting 522.5 km; 0.8 inch per km.
